From dd6e8eebb4216793734cac3a3e9823cee4e218cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:22:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a containment refusal ends only its board's
 round; never abandon the sync watcher [daveey]

Example incident: ContainmentRefused from certify_page escaped sync_board -> sync_all_once
-> run_forever, killed kanban_sync_watcher, and after 5 rapid restarts the supervisor gave up
for good. Every board on the example gateways stopped syncing in repeated incidents and
stayed down until each gateway restarted; dispatchers held all claims on sync_first_round.

- sync_all_once catches ContainmentRefused per board (kanban_sync_refusal): nothing from the
  page is applied, the cursor is kept, the board backs off 60 s doubling to 15 min, one ERROR
  per distinct refusal; other boards keep syncing. certify_page/remember stay strict.
- _spawn_supervised: tasks in _SUPERVISED_SLOW_RETRY_SECS (kanban_sync_watcher: 300 s) respawn
  with a fresh budget after giving up; on_give_up still fires first.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_refusal.py and tests/gateway/test_supervised_slow_retry.py
fail on c9e2b66d13 and pass here; 9 sync/containment/supervisor files: 198 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
